Q4. What is the role of Synopsys ICC2?

ICC2 is a physical implementation tool used to perform floorplanning, placement, CTS, routing, optimization, and other physical design tasks.

Q5. What is the role of PrimeTime?

PrimeTime is used for Static Timing Analysis (STA). It analyzes timing paths, setup and hold checks, slack, and timing violations using timing constraints and cell/interconnect delays.

Q6. What is the difference between Design Compiler and ICC2?

Design Compiler synthesizes RTL into a gate-level netlist. ICC2 uses the netlist and physical design information to implement the design and generate the physical layout.

Q7. What is floorplanning?

Floorplanning is the first major physical design step. It defines the core and die area, places macros, considers I/O pins and blockages, and prepares the design for power planning and placement.


